# RegEngine — packages imported only by modules behind EXPERIMENTAL_ROUTERS
# (server/router_policy.py), which never mount in production (WI-06, 2026-11-04).
#
# Determined by a static transitive import trace from server/main.py over the
# repository (docs/plans/TECH_DEBT_REMEDIATION_PRD_2026-10-28.md, WI-06 status):
# every other third-party distribution is also reached from an always-mounted
# or production-allowlisted module and stays in requirements.in. langchain,
# openai, llama-cloud, pytesseract and pdf2image are reached from
# services/ingestion/app/regulation_parser.py, normalization.py,
# regengine_ingestion/llm/client.py and services/shared/document_extract, so
# they stay.
#
# Constrained by requirements.lock. The constraint is passed on the command
# line, not in this file: Dependabot fetches a constraint file only when its
# name ends in .txt or .in, and its whole pip run aborts when it cannot open
# one. Compile with:
#   pip-compile --allow-unsafe --constraint=requirements.lock --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements-experimental.lock requirements-experimental.in

# services/ingestion/app/qr_decoder.py (experimental router "qr_decoder");
# imported lazily with a 503 fallback, so tests run without it.
